# DTF tier manifest: rpm-repodata-regeneration-metric  (#4174)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a real dnf client.
#
# #4174 extracts the RPM repodata fingerprint cache (#2521) into a
# format-agnostic metadata revision cache and gives it shared metrics:
# ak_repo_metadata_regenerations_total{format,scope},
# ak_repo_metadata_regeneration_seconds{format} and
# ak_repo_metadata_cache_requests_total{format,result}.
#
# Oracle (oracle.sh): a hosted RPM root of 300 synthetic packages (rows
# seeded straight into Postgres: the render reads rows, not package bytes),
# then
#   * 20 concurrent cold repomd.xml GETs: all 200, one body, and exactly one
#     regenerations sample for format="rpm" (RED on 1.11.5: the cache renders
#     once but reports nothing, so the counter is absent);
#   * warm repeats add cache hits, no regeneration;
#   * one more package: the next GET serves a new body and the counter moves
#     by exactly one;
#   * `dnf makecache` in a Fedora client accepts the served metadata.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle sends bursts of GETs.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.dnf"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
